SUMMARY:Noël Acadien au Village
LOCATION:LARC's Acadian Village\, 200 Greenleaf Dr\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:Lafayette's big Christmas lights festival: about half a million
  lights across the Acadian Village\, including the lit-up chapel\, plus ho
 liday displays\, live music\, carnival rides\, local food\, photos with Sa
 nta and the Christmas Store.\n\nTickets: $10 in advance at area ShopRite s
 tores\, $11 online (plus a fee) or $12 at the gate. Kids 2 and under get i
 n free.\n\nIt's a fundraiser for LARC\, a Lafayette nonprofit that support
 s people with intellectual and developmental disabilities. Dates here are 
 from LARC's 2026 announcements\; check the village's website or Facebook p
 age for weather closures.\n\nhttps://acadianvillage.org/noel-acadien-au-vi
 llage/
